From d8bfc7b980bdeb5e3aac4710e839eec5af312d9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:37:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution settings: options named after the phases

The options placing each phase in the mixed mode are renamed after their
phase, with the same suffix: --finite-elements-execution (-fex),
--behaviours-execution (-bhx), --linear-solvers-execution (-lsx, formerly
--linear-solver-device, which suggested a GPU) and
--post-processings-execution (-ppx). The names do not collide with the
options of mfem-mgis-examples and mm-opera-hpc; the former names are not
kept (the options only exist in this branch).
